fifa2010wc patch 0001 for ReXGlue v0.11.0 (a3e1d82): configurable function table base

Project A numbering: 0003 function-table-base (J2 step A3, docs/J2_A3_FUNCTION_TABLE.md).

v0.11.0 puts the dispatch table of every module right after its image, at
image_base + image_size. The table of default.xex can then run into the image of the
module loaded after it. This patch adds the per binary codegen key function_table_base
and carries it to the runtime:
- codegen: the key, its validation (64 KiB aligned, inside 0x80000000-0x8FFFFFFF),
  REX_FUNC_TABLE_BASE in the generated header, the lookup in _indirect_call.inja and
  PPCImage::function_table_base in the generated init;
- runtime: FunctionDispatcher and GuestAddressSpace::InitializeFunctionTable take the
  table base; the dispatcher refuses any overlap between images and tables, and a moved
  table must land on free pages of the XEX heap;
- without the key, the table stays where upstream puts it.

Provenance: adapted from patch 0003-function-table-base.patch of
CalinGraphics/fifa-world-cup-2010-recompiled, commit 498d18a, written for rexglue-sdk
bd833a2. BSD 3-Clause License, Copyright (c) 2026, Miertescu Stefan-Calin; the notice is
reproduced in THIRD_PARTY.md. Rewritten for v0.11.0 (other file layout and names).
Added here: 64 bit range ends, the check of a table against its own image, the free page
check, codegen validation and the unit tests.

Not touched: XEX loading and decryption (src/filesystem/xex.cpp, src/kernel/xex_module.cpp,
thirdparty/excrypt). Check: grep '^diff --git' on this file.

